#
# The compositor owns the displays: every output that exports display_v1, up
# to two (the mailbox framebuffer and the SPI panel), one viewport of the
# desktop each. It maps a scanout output's Frames and writes a flush output's
# data area. It is also the only consumer of the USB HID component's input
# interface: it reads the descriptor and the state of each device the
# component serves, and the events arrive on the interface's io-channel. An
# image without the HID component leaves the input import not granted and the
# compositor runs without input.
uses display_v1 via every max 2 { describe, get_mode, frames, flush }
uses input_v1 via component usb_hid { descriptor, snapshot }
# In an image with the log server, the compositor's trace goes to it
# on the interface's io-channel instead of the serial channel, which the log
# server holds; elsewhere the import stays unlinked and the compositor holds the
# serial channel itself (`serial = true`).
uses log_v1 via component log_server { flush }
